# Step 1: the tools the model may call, from the catalogue. `format =
# "tools"` answers one definition per capability — the name the model sees
# (dots as underscores), the description, the input as a JSON Schema, and a
# binding that names the capability — so no rule here carries a copy of
# what `_tools` declares. The definitions are data in the envelope, visible
# in the trace, and the same whichever model is asked.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path in ["/tools", "/ask", "/order", "/order-bad"]
  WITH names  = ["stock.check", "price.quote"],
       format = "tools",
       into   = "_tools"
  EXEC "txco://caps/list"
